 "title": "An Infinite Descent into Pure Mathematics",
 "byline": "Clive Newstead \u00b7 version 0.7 (25 June 2026), pre-publication edition of the forthcoming first edition, CC BY-SA 4.0",
 "note": "Your Drive had version 0.5 (2022); this page follows version 0.7, downloaded from infinitedescent.org into the same folder. End-of-chapter exercise sections, hints/solutions and the LaTeX appendix are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "An introduction to proof and pure mathematics for first-year undergraduates that teaches logical reasoning, proof-writing and problem-solving together. Part I covers the core: propositional logic and quantifiers, sets, functions, induction from Peano\u2019s axioms, relations and equivalence relations, and finite and countable sets. Part II tours topics: elementary number theory and modular arithmetic, enumerative combinatorics, real numbers with inequalities, completeness and series, cardinal arithmetic, discrete probability, and orders, lattices and inductively defined sets. Appendices give proof-writing advice and foundational constructions of the number systems."
}